<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/binomial-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "For n independent Bernoulli trials with common success probability p in [0,1], the probability of k successes is choose(n,k) p to the k times (1−p) to the (n−k), for 0 ≤ k ≤ n, with endpoint probabilities interpreted by continuity."@en .
