<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/probability-distributions> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "In a uniform sample of size n without replacement from m successes and N−m failures, the probability of k successes is choose(m,k) choose(N−m,n−k) divided by choose(N,n). Here 0 ≤ n ≤ N, 0 ≤ m ≤ N and max(0,n−(N−m)) ≤ k ≤ min(n,m); the mass is zero outside the support."@en .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/scheme/statistics> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Hypergeometric probability mass formula"@en .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/vocab/containsSymbol> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/binomial-coefficient> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-mass-formula> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/vocab/uses> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/ontomath-pro-e867> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/probability-distributions> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "For a valid uniform sample without replacement, sum the count of subsets with exactly k successes over all feasible k. Vandermonde's identity gives the total number choose(N,n) of subsets of size n, so the masses sum to one."@en .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/scheme/statistics> .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Vandermonde normalization of hypergeometric mass"@en .
<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/hypergeometric-normalization> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/vocab/uses> <https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/vandermonde-convolution> .
