<https://curricula.live/id/formal-sciences/concept/modal-necessitation-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The inference rule that licenses deriving necessity of a theorem. In a normal modal logic the premise is a theorem without undischarged assumptions."@en .
